il"},{"n":"Canton of Petit-Bourg","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":16.184444,"lo":-61.582222,"d":7243,"ds":"The Canton of Petit-Bourg is a canton in the Arrondissement of Basse-Terre on the island of Guadeloupe.","wpu":"Canton of Petit-Bourg","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Locator_map_of_Kanton_Petit-Bourg_2018.png/960px-Locator_map_of_Kanton_Petit-Bourg_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hôtel de Ville, Petit-Bourg","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":16.1915,"lo":-61.5905,"d":7343,"ds":"The Hôtel de Ville (French pronunciation: [otɛl də vil], City Hall) is a municipal building in Petit-Bourg, Guadeloupe in the Caribbean Sea, standing on Rue Victor Schoelcher.","wpu":"Hôtel de Ville, Petit-Bourg","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Mairie_de_Petit-Bourg.JPG/960px-Mairie_de_Petit-Bourg.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Pointe-à-Pitre (French pronunciation: [pwɛ̃tapitʁ]; Guadeloupean Creole: Pwentapit, [pwɛ̃tapit], or simply Lapwent, [lapwɛ̃t]) is the second most populous commune of Guadeloupe (after Les Abymes). Guadeloupe is an overseas region and department of France located in the Lesser Antilles, of which it is a sous-préfecture, being the seat of the arrondissement of Pointe-à-Pitre. Although Pointe-à-Pitre is not Guadeloupe's administrative capital (that distinction goes to Basse-Terre), it is nonetheless the region's economic capital.","wpu":"Pointe-à-Pitre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Pointe-%C3%A0-Pitre.JPG/960px-Pointe-%C3%A0-Pitre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}